Yes, it would need to make a copy of the callback and context before the destroy call, like this, for example:
```c
	struct bt_mesh_adv adv = *BT_MESH_ADV(buf);

	net_buf_destroy(buf);

	bt_mesh_adv_send_end(0, &adv);
```

I think this line needs to be reinstated like:

bt_mesh_adv_send_end(0, adv);

As it seems to not inform the calling function it has release provisioning process.
